# Episode stream for `mm-cli memory consolidate --input bench/memory/episodes.jsonl`
# and the corpus `mm-cli memory eval` ingests before grading (plan §7, §8).
#
# One JSON object per line; `#` lines are comments and are skipped by
# `mm_memory::consolidate::read_episodes`.
#
# `ref` is the stable external reference. It is REQUIRED: the memory's ULID is
# derived from it (`mm_memory::model::ref_ulid`), so the same file ingested twice
# produces the same ids and the second run adds nothing. `topic` is the
# consolidation key — episodes sharing a topic are folded into one semantic
# memory — and `entities` are shared within a topic so the entity graph has edges
# to walk. The `rust` entity appears in two topics on purpose: it is the bridge
# the graph channel uses to reach a memory that shares no query words.
#
# Categories follow LongMemEval/LoCoMo: multi_session (recall across sessions),
# temporal (when something held), knowledge_update (a fact that changed), and
# abstention (what cannot be answered).
#
# All twelve `valid_from` instants are recent, so none of these episodes falls
# below `thresholds.toml`'s retention floor on the day the gate runs.

